* For example, real-time voice services \(telephone calls\) can only sustain a maximum latency between the end points before interactive speech becomes difficult. This maximum latency between endpoints translates to two demands from the network;
  * 1\. Minimising hop by hop latency as a voice packet flows across the network infrastructure.
  * 2\. Minimising jitter in the packets arriving in order to minimise the de-jitter buffer needed at the receiver \(which adds latency\).

